PICONIX VI - EXACT COMMANDS (NOT GNU VIM)

Start on MCP PTY: terminal_open({"command":"vi /tmp/test.txt"}).
Then terminal_read({}) to inspect screen and current mode.
Only direct /tmp/NAME or /etc/NAME RAM files; max 2048 bytes.

NORMAL MODE (press terminal_send({"key":"ESC"}) first)
  h j k l / arrow keys    move cursor
  0 / $                   line start / line end
  i                       insert before cursor
  a                       insert after cursor
  o                       open line below, enter INSERT
  x                       delete character at cursor
  d then d                delete current line (two key presses)
  :w + ENTER              save; stay in editor
  :q + ENTER              quit only if unmodified
  :q! + ENTER             discard edits and quit
  :wq + ENTER             save then quit
  :x + ENTER              save then quit
  :help + ENTER           brief command hint
  :%s/OLD/NEW/g + ENTER   replace literal OLD with NEW in whole file
                            (no regex, no escaped slash; <=2048 bytes)

INSERT MODE: terminal_send({"text":"hello"}) inserts characters;
ENTER inserts newline; BACKSPACE deletes backward; ESC returns to
NORMAL. Do NOT use : commands while in INSERT mode.

MCP sequence: ESC -> send text ":%s/1000/100/g" -> ENTER ->
terminal_read({}) -> ESC -> send ":wq" -> ENTER ->
execute_command({"command":"cat /tmp/test.txt"}) for verification.
Commands :set, undo, /pattern and regex substitution are NOT
implemented. :help displays a brief command hint. Do not guess full Vim commands.

terminal_read returns "unchanged" if screen has not changed since
last successful read; it does NOT establish whether file was saved.
Use cat for independent verification. Avoid blind retries after TCP
errors; check the file before repeating a potentially modifying step.
